## Fixed and verified this session (v0.11.81 → v0.11.82, uncommitted)

1. **tcp dlm_scaling collapse (8/16/32, deterministic)** — RULE-4 chain: DLM exonerated (dlm_us=0.25ms); the cost was the per-unlink synchronous eager ifree chain (log_force+drain+flush, 17-33ms) plus per-modify target flushes, amplified by the LIO-on-ext4 rig honoring flushes (SCST rigs no-op them — why caw* passed). Fixes: `flush_epoch` ticks without the device flush under `fua_disable` (the flush was the **epoch clock** — proven when skipping the call froze P68-EVDECIDE into an undurable-skip stale-base storm), `ifree_eager_durable=0`, and a coalesced background **destage kick** (10ms debounce, async force+AIL push). 8/tcp: 90s DNF → 34-37s PASS.
2. **Leaf-hash holes** (lookup ENOENT with readdir OK) — `dir_leaf_rebuild=1` default; and the rebuild's disk-snapshot union made **in-core-only** (union was delete-unsafe: resurrected renamed-away dirents, proven via P26-REBUILD-OK `comm=mv`).
3. **Cross-incarnation reload adopt** guard (P34G) — later ruled wrong-sided by the consult; scheduled for replacement.

## The open front (Phase A ready to implement)

The eager chain was secretly the linchpin of reuse convergence: with it gone, peers created 112 files inside a directory **freed 9 minutes earlier** (cached shells + positive dentries bypassed every validation layer; parallel universes on one name). GPT consult (RULE 5) produced a complete design: first-protective-tenure incarnation certification with poison/ESTALE semantics + parent-tenure-epoch d_revalidate. The full decision matrix, implementation plan (flag bit 24, reload-poison, op-entry checks, shell retirement), and verification recipe are in `state.md`, which also carries the power-loss recovery procedure. This family likely also explains task #1 (tcp/16 payload-in-dirblock) and the rv rename-visibility flake.

